SOAPBOX: I caught the flu just few days before contest, so it was difficult to talk proper on Saturday.
SOAPBOX: Also the propagation on Saturday was strange — couldn't hear anything from first skip in 2000km range from East - usually there are very loud UA9, UN7 stations but even well known big-guns was not audible at all! On Sunday it was all opens well as should be.
SOAPBOX: Perhaps it's time to start consider about changing station location — electrical noise from the East direction has increased significantly in last year or so... For the first time ever (!), I could not hear anyone from VK/ZL and missed a lot of usual easy to get far Asian's DX, unfortunately.
SOAPBOX: But in any case, I really enjoyed participating, even though SSB isn't my favorite operating mode.
